From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3: no wallpaper button when no app picks wallpapers

The home screen's edit mode (a long press on the home screen) offers
"Wallpapers", "Widgets" and "Home settings". Nothing on the device handles
ACTION_SET_WALLPAPER (no wallpaper picker; the wallpaper is the built-in white
picture, which no window shows, frameworks/base 0034): tapping the button
opened nothing (Test V45); the code then shows a toast, "app not found".

The button, and its action for accessibility services, are shown only when an
app resolves the button's intent: a picker installed later brings them back
once the home screen is created again. Edit mode keeps its two other buttons.

--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/Utilities.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/Utilities.java
@@ -560,6 +560,20 @@
     public static boolean isPowerSaverOn(Context context) {
         PowerManager powerManager = (PowerManager) context.getSystemService(Context.POWER_SERVICE);
         return powerManager.isPowerSaveMode();
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * PW3: whether an app handles the intent of the wallpaper button
+     * (Launcher#onClickWallpaperPicker). The device has none: the button did nothing when
+     * tapped (Test V45), so it is not shown.
+     */
+    public static boolean hasWallpaperPicker(Context context) {
+        Intent intent = new Intent(Intent.ACTION_SET_WALLPAPER);
+        String pickerPackage = context.getString(R.string.wallpaper_picker_package);
+        if (!TextUtils.isEmpty(pickerPackage)) {
+            intent.setPackage(pickerPackage);
+        }
+        return context.getPackageManager().resolveActivity(intent, 0) != null;
     }
 
     public static boolean isWallpaperAllowed(Context context) {
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/Launcher.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/Launcher.java
@@ -1325,6 +1325,10 @@
 
         // Bind wallpaper button actions
         View wallpaperButton = findViewById(R.id.wallpaper_button);
+        // PW3: hidden when no app can pick a wallpaper (Utilities.hasWallpaperPicker()).
+        if (!Utilities.hasWallpaperPicker(this)) {
+            wallpaperButton.setVisibility(View.GONE);
+        }
         new OverviewButtonClickListener(ControlType.WALLPAPER_BUTTON) {
             @Override
             public void handleViewClick(View view) {
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/accessibility/OverviewAccessibilityDelegate.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/accessibility/OverviewAccessibilityDelegate.java
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
         Context context = host.getContext();
         info.addAction(new AccessibilityAction(OVERVIEW, context.getText(OVERVIEW)));
 
-        if (Utilities.isWallpaperAllowed(context)) {
+        if (Utilities.isWallpaperAllowed(context) && Utilities.hasWallpaperPicker(context)) {
             info.addAction(new AccessibilityAction(WALLPAPERS, context.getText(WALLPAPERS)));
         }
         info.addAction(new AccessibilityAction(WIDGETS, context.getText(WIDGETS)));
